WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.760
- All right, before we wrap up the hour,

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:04.450
I wanna share one last story
I hope will make you smile.

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:05.402
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:05.402 --> 00:00:06.235
(bright upbeat music)

00:00:06.235 --> 00:00:08.230
(audience applauds)

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:09.590
As we approach Father's Day,

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:11.330
I wanna tell you about a mama in Detroit

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:12.980
who's making sure the whole world knows

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.210
just how incredible her man
is as a husband and dad.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:19.990
So check out this very
sweet TikTok she posted

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.350
- [Eden] Ever since having our
baby, my husband makes sure

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.740
that I get eight hours to sleep every day,

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:27.240
which means he usually gets about four.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.530
At first I felt guilty,

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.730
but he insisted and
explained it to me like this.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:34.750
There are so many burdens
that you carry that I cannot.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.730
All the burdens of
pregnancy, birth, recovery,

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.090
breastfeeding, lack of
sleep and late nights

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:42.960
with the baby is the only
burden I can take from you.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.264
So why in the world would I not?

00:00:44.264 --> 00:00:47.052
(gentle guitar music)

00:00:47.052 --> 00:00:48.475
(audience applauds)

00:00:48.475 --> 00:00:50.693
- That is incredible.

00:00:50.693 --> 00:00:51.760
We have this couple

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.260
on the line right now watching

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.950
on WXYZ Channel 7.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.062
Hi, Eden.

00:00:57.062 --> 00:00:57.895
(audience applauds)

00:00:57.895 --> 00:00:58.728
Hi, Jonathan.

00:00:58.728 --> 00:01:00.640
(audience applauds)

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:02.560
Look at your beautiful kiddos.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:03.393
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:03.393 --> 00:01:04.880
So, Jonathan, way to step up

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.800
and just make all dads look so bad.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.970
Why is this so important to you?

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:12.200
- Yeah, we really just learned so much

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.900
after having our first child
Zion here who is almost two.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.580
And one of the things we
learned is that there's just

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:21.058
a lot of things that
parents don't talk about.

00:01:21.058 --> 00:01:21.891
- And one of those things-

00:01:21.891 --> 00:01:22.724
(Zion cooing)

00:01:22.724 --> 00:01:23.695
- Bye, bye, bye, bye.

00:01:23.695 --> 00:01:25.460
- One of those things is just
that people don't really talk

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:28.450
about how difficult the recovery can be

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:31.320
for the mom after having a baby.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.040
And they're going through that recovery

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.040
while also having to
take care of the baby.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:39.910
So after having our
second child here, Ezra,

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:41.650
we just really wanted to
improve the situation.

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:44.400
So I really focused on making
sure she got enough sleep

00:01:45.544 --> 00:01:47.210
the whole night since

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:49.303
that is this thing I was able to help with

00:01:49.303 --> 00:01:50.553
while she was recovering.

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:53.330
- That is so cool, man.

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:57.260
Eden, what did that feel
like to just be supported?

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:00.690
- I mean, so after I had
Zion, our first child,

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:02.830
I got really bad postpartum depression,

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:06.230
and I think a lot of that had
to do with the lack of sleep.

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:08.900
And so, this time around
Jonathan was really determined

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:12.500
to make sure that my recovery
went as smoothly as possible,

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.180
which for me meant getting more sleep.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:17.250
So, yeah, and it just really showed me

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:20.120
how much he loved me and cares for me.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:21.207
- Yeah, and loves your kiddos.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:24.620
It's such a beautiful, beautiful thing.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.458
I am liking your post right now.

00:02:26.458 --> 00:02:28.367
(audience applauds)

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:29.230
And that's not all.

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:31.930
Our season-long partner,
Pilot Pen makers of G2,

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:33.480
the go-to pin of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:36.240
wanna honor ultimate
overachievers just like y'all.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.347
So they're gonna be writing
you a check for $1000.

00:02:38.347 --> 00:02:40.626
(audience applauds)

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:42.267
- Thank you.
Thank you.

00:02:42.267 --> 00:02:44.165
- Thank you guys so much.

00:02:44.165 --> 00:02:45.260
(audience applauds)

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:46.333
Nothing but good health,

00:02:46.333 --> 00:02:47.704
and God bless you and your little kiddos.

00:02:47.704 --> 00:02:48.537
(audience applauds)

